WEBVTT

NOTE
Canonical narration text; deterministic paragraph-window timing.
Text and terminology reviewed against the chapter packet on 2026-07-29.
Publication still requires final listening review against the authorized narration master.

1
00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:03.930
Long-lived AI systems do not merely retrieve context.

2
00:00:03.930 --> 00:00:09.060
They mutate durable memory through stores, branches, indexes, caches, summaries, replicas,

3
00:00:09.060 --> 00:00:14.189
and recovery paths. A clean-looking prompt can still come from a

4
00:00:14.189 --> 00:00:19.318
mixed snapshot, an uncommitted write, a stale index, a foreign branch,

5
00:00:19.318 --> 00:00:24.447
or a derivative whose source was revoked. This chapter treats context

6
00:00:24.447 --> 00:00:29.576
as accountable state. A Context Transaction binds the principal, purpose, operation,

7
00:00:29.576 --> 00:00:33.773
base snapshot, branch, mounts, authority, rights, isolation, durability, budget,

8
00:00:33.773 --> 00:00:38.902
and support ceiling to the actual pre-state and every attempted, applied,

9
00:00:38.902 --> 00:00:41.700
visible, replayed, recovered, or indeterminate post-state.

10
00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:48.129
The transaction begins with an observed snapshot, not a friendly name

11
00:00:48.129 --> 00:00:54.057
or timestamp. It binds exact object versions, content and index epochs,

12
00:00:54.057 --> 00:00:59.447
causal parents, branch, mount policy, provenance, taint, leases, caches, backups,

13
00:00:59.447 --> 00:01:05.375
and open obligations. The request declares intended reads, writes, derivations, deletions,

14
00:01:05.375 --> 00:01:10.226
and revocations, but the receipt records what actually happened.

15
00:01:10.226 --> 00:01:15.616
Purpose-bound mounts distinguish read, write, derive, delete, share, export, train,

16
00:01:15.616 --> 00:01:19.927
and execute permission. No cache, summary, branch, replica,

17
00:01:19.927 --> 00:01:23.700
or restore route may widen that envelope.

18
00:01:24.200 --> 00:01:30.062
Commit is a lifecycle, not a success boolean. Requested, admitted, prepared,

19
00:01:30.062 --> 00:01:34.325
applied, durably committed, consumer-visible, replayed, recovered, compensated, aborted,

20
00:01:34.325 --> 00:01:39.654
and indeterminate are different states. Content, indexes, provenance, taint, rights,

21
00:01:39.654 --> 00:01:45.516
derivative edges, deletion obligations, caches, and audit references commit atomically only

22
00:01:45.516 --> 00:01:51.378
inside the declared boundary. Conflicts, lost updates, write skew, stale indexes,

23
00:01:51.378 --> 00:01:56.174
retry duplicates, partial writes, and uncertain participants remain explicit.

24
00:01:56.174 --> 00:02:02.036
Crash recovery must return to the declared durable frontier and compare

25
00:02:02.036 --> 00:02:04.700
independently observed state after restart.

26
00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:10.246
Consider a source correction on branch B. A transaction reads snapshot

27
00:02:10.246 --> 00:02:14.375
forty-one through a purpose-bound mount, writes a corrected object,

28
00:02:14.375 --> 00:02:19.422
derives a summary and embedding, and invalidates an exact response cache.

29
00:02:19.422 --> 00:02:23.092
A concurrent branch changes the same semantic object,

30
00:02:23.092 --> 00:02:28.138
so silent last-writer-wins is forbidden. The transaction rebases or preserves both

31
00:02:28.138 --> 00:02:32.726
branches. Taint from the corrected source follows the summary, embedding,

32
00:02:32.726 --> 00:02:37.313
cache key, and downstream route. If deletion is later requested,

33
00:02:37.313 --> 00:02:41.901
closure walks live objects, indexes, caches, replicas, exports, and backups.

34
00:02:41.901 --> 00:02:46.947
An unreachable backup remains an owned residual; it cannot be relabeled

35
00:02:46.947 --> 00:02:49.700
as physical erasure or model forgetting.

36
00:02:50.200 --> 00:02:55.109
Caching makes the distinction especially important. Prefix caching reuses compatible model

37
00:02:55.109 --> 00:03:00.017
state and still produces a new answer. Response caching returns a

38
00:03:00.017 --> 00:03:04.926
prior answer. An exact response key therefore closes over request, consumer,

39
00:03:04.926 --> 00:03:09.834
model, decoding, tools, sources, schema, locale, time, authority, purpose, policy, rights,

40
00:03:09.834 --> 00:03:14.743
side-effect state, verifier, and dependency versions. A semantic cache weakens the

41
00:03:14.743 --> 00:03:19.652
match further: similarity is only an approximate route candidate. Dynamic facts,

42
00:03:19.652 --> 00:03:23.222
personalized decisions, high-impact advice, security actions, rights-sensitive material,

43
00:03:23.222 --> 00:03:28.130
and side-effecting operations normally require fresh evaluation. Every hit discloses whether

44
00:03:28.130 --> 00:03:31.700
compatible prefill or a prior answer was reused.

45
00:03:32.200 --> 00:03:37.700
This design can still become transaction theater. A perfect log may

46
00:03:37.700 --> 00:03:43.200
describe bytes that never became durable. A database can protect records

47
00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:47.200
without preserving semantic identity, taint, or erasure categories.

48
00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:52.700
Deleting storage does not establish behavioral forgetting, influence removal, privacy protection,

49
00:03:52.700 --> 00:03:58.200
or removal from external descendants. The strongest current checks are finite:

50
00:03:58.200 --> 00:04:03.700
three valid and six invalid store fixtures, two valid and four

51
00:04:03.700 --> 00:04:09.200
invalid event sequences, seventy-eight rejected mutations, and one bounded historical-project lifecycle.

52
00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:13.700
They establish record and route consequences, not concurrency, serializability,

53
00:04:13.700 --> 00:04:17.700
crash-safe deployed storage, complete invalidation, or useful memory.

54
00:04:18.200 --> 00:04:23.056
The core remains Design rationale at argument support and blocked after

55
00:04:23.056 --> 00:04:27.913
a full attempt. Its maximum inference is a bounded finite partially

56
00:04:27.913 --> 00:04:32.328
observed world-model result only—no open-world truth, general memory transfer, deployment,

57
00:04:32.328 --> 00:04:37.184
or chapter-core promotion. A valid context transaction says which state transition

58
00:04:37.184 --> 00:04:42.040
occurred within its declared boundary. It does not say that the

59
00:04:42.040 --> 00:04:46.455
context is true, sufficient, safe, or useful. The next chapter,

60
00:04:46.455 --> 00:04:50.429
Verification Bandwidth and Context Adequacy, asks that separate question:

61
00:04:50.429 --> 00:04:54.844
whether the system has enough evidence, tools, comparisons, contradiction search,

62
00:04:54.844 --> 00:04:59.700
and reviewer capacity to justify the claim it wants to make.
